1
00:05:46,363 --> 00:05:52,363
Sometimes dreams come back to life.

2
00:11:32,727 --> 00:11:38,727
The Rookie is a drama, family film directed by John Lee Hancock.

3
00:17:19,090 --> 00:17:25,090
Jim Morris never made it out of the minor leagues before a shoulder
injury ended his pitching career twelve years ago.

4
00:23:05,454 --> 00:23:11,454
Now a married-with-children high-school chemistry teacher and baseball coach in Texas, Jim's team makes a deal
with him: if they win the district championship, Jim will try out with a major-league organization.

5
00:28:51,818 --> 00:28:57,818
The bet proves incentive enough for the team, and they go from worst to first,
making it to state for the first time in the history of the school.

6
00:34:38,181 --> 00:34:44,181
Jim, forced to live up to his end of the deal, is nearly laughed off the try-out field--until he gets onto the mound, where he confounds the
scouts (and himself) by clocking successive 98 mph fastballs, good enough for a minor-league contract with the Tampa Bay Devil Rays.

7
00:40:24,545 --> 00:40:30,545
Jim's still got a lot of pitches to throw before he makes it to The Show, but with
his big-league dreams revived, there's no telling where he could go.

8
00:46:10,909 --> 00:46:16,909
Jimmy Morris, played by Dennis Quaid.

9
00:51:57,272 --> 00:52:03,272
Lorri Morris, played by Rachel Griffiths.

10
00:57:43,636 --> 00:57:49,636
Joaquin 'Wack' Campos, played by Jay Hernandez.

11
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:36,000
Olline, played by Beth Grant.

12
01:09:16,363 --> 01:09:22,363
Hunter Morris, played by Angus T. Jones.

13
01:15:02,727 --> 01:15:08,727
Jim Morris Sr., played by Brian Cox.

14
01:20:49,090 --> 01:20:55,090
The Rookie is a 2002 American sports drama film directed by John
Lee Hancock and produced by Walt Disney Pictures.

15
01:26:35,454 --> 01:26:41,454
It is based on the true story of Jim Morris who
debuted in Major League Baseball at age 35.

16
01:32:21,818 --> 01:32:27,818
The film stars Dennis Quaid as Morris, alongside
Rachel Griffiths, Jay Hernandez, Angus T.

17
01:38:08,181 --> 01:38:14,181
Jones, and Brian Cox.

18
01:43:54,545 --> 01:44:00,545
It was released in the United States on March 29, 2002.

19
01:49:40,909 --> 01:49:46,909
The movie was filmed in 2.40:1 widescreen.

20
01:55:27,272 --> 01:55:33,272
The film explores themes of sports, parent child
relationship, baseball, life's dream, growing up.

21
02:01:13,636 --> 02:01:19,636
The tone is emotional.
